.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_KDF-KRB5KDF 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_KDF-KRB5KDF
.Nd The RFC3961 Krb5 KDF EVP_KDF implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing the
.Sy KRB5KDF
KDF through the
.Sy EVP_KDF
API.
.Pp
The EVP_KDF-KRB5KDF algorithm implements the key derivation function
defined in RFC 3961, section 5.1 and is used by Krb5 to derive session
keys.
Three inputs are required to perform key derivation: a cipher, (for
example AES-128-CBC), the initial key, and a constant.
.Ss Identity
"KRB5KDF" is the name for this implementation; it can be used with the
.Xr EVP_KDF_fetch 3
function.
.Ss Supported parameters
The supported parameters are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqproperties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_PROPERTIES Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqcipher" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_CIPHER Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqkey" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
These parameters work as described in
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 .
.It \(dqconstant" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_CONSTANT Ns ) <octet string>
This parameter sets the constant value for the KDF. If a value is
already set, the contents are replaced.
.El
.Sh NOTES
A context for KRB5KDF can be obtained by calling:
.Bd -literal
 EVP_KDF *kdf = EVP_KDF_fetch(NULL, "KRB5KDF", NULL);
 EVP_KDF_CTX *kctx = EVP_KDF_CTX_new(kdf);
.Ed
.Pp
The output length of the KRB5KDF derivation is specified via the
.Em keylen
parameter to the
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3
function, and MUST match the key length for the chosen cipher or an
error is returned.
Moreover, the constant's length must not exceed the block size of the
cipher.
Since the KRB5KDF output length depends on the chosen cipher, calling
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_get_kdf_size 3
to obtain the requisite length returns the correct length only after the
cipher is set.
Prior to that
.Sy EVP_MAX_KEY_LENGTH
is returned.
The caller must allocate a buffer of the correct length for the chosen
cipher, and pass that buffer to the
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3
function along with that length.
.Sh EXAMPLES
This example derives a key using the AES-128-CBC cipher:
.Bd -literal
 EVP_KDF *kdf;
 EVP_KDF_CTX *kctx;
 unsigned char key[16] = "01234...";
 unsigned char constant[] = "I'm a constant";
 unsigned char out[16];
 size_t outlen = sizeof(out);
 OSSL_PARAM params[4], *p = params;

 kdf = EVP_KDF_fetch(NULL, "KRB5KDF", NULL);
 kctx = EVP_KDF_CTX_new(kdf);
 EVP_KDF_free(kdf);

 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_utf8_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_CIPHER,
                                         SN_aes_128_cbc,
                                         strlen(SN_aes_128_cbc));
 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY,
                                          key, (size_t)16);
 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_CONSTANT,
                                          constant, strlen(constant));
 *p = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
 if (EVP_KDF_derive(kctx, out, outlen, params) <= 0)
     /* Error */

 EVP_KDF_CTX_free(kctx);
.Ed
.Sh CONFORMING TO
RFC 3961
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_free 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_get_kdf_size 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3 ,
.Xr EVP_KDF 3
